# Test for G208, Inhibit Driver.
#
# Add-on board is needed, manual test procedure below.
#
# NAND Inputs: AT/AU
# Out: Inhibit loop AR/AP
#      Current determining resistor: AN/AS
#
# NAND Inputs: AD/AU
# Out: Inhibit loop AF/AH
#      Current determining resistor: AJ/AE
#
# The 'config' key describes how the tested board has it connections.
#
# 'p' - power pin, do nothing
# 'i' - input pin on tested board
# 'o' - output pin on tested board
# 'O' - output pin on tested board, open collector
# 'd' - pull down net on tested board
# 'g' - pin should be grounded on tested board
# '-' - pin should not be used, don't care and it will be electrically disconnected

#
#       AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#       ABCDEFHJKLMNPRSTUVABCDEFHJKLMNPRSTUV
config='pppi-----------ii-ppp---------------'
# Test MB0 inhibit line (output AR/AP). Measure at AS vs Inh-
vector='---0-----------1T-------------------'
# Test MB0 inhibit line (output AF/AH). Measure at AE vs Inh-
vector='---1-----------0T-------------------'

input-current-low='-0.0mA'
input-current-high='-2.0mA'
input-current-margin='1.5mA'
input-voltage-high='-10mV'
input-voltage-low='-3700mV'
toggles='100000'


####################################################################################
#
# Test Jig Instructions & Usage
# Making a load board for testing adapter for testing pin DA
# This setup gives an approximation of the inhibit current setup in which a G208
# operates. A resistor sets the current in conjunction with a DC supply.
# Inspect the core module for the required inhibit current. It will be approx. 300mA
# The nominal inhibit supply in the PDP-8 is 37VDC.
# Choose a combination of resistor and supply voltage to achieve something close
# to the required inhibit current.
#
# The simplest way to construct is with a spare connector PCB.
#
# Fit the two 40 pin headers for connector A
#
# Connect the following (unshielded wire to allow oscilloscope to be hooked on)
# These are taking the place of the inhibit loop.
# AE - AH
# AP - AR
#
# Connect 100R 5W resistors between. These are the current determining resistors.
# They'll carry a large current but only for a brief pulse. Lower wattage may work.
# AE - AJ
# AN - AS
#
# Two flying leads to connect the inhibit supply. Use an (ideally) isolated bench/lab
# supply set to approx 30V.
# AK - Red   (supply +ve)
# AL - Black (supply -ve)
#
# Use and additional (short!) ribbon cable to place the modified connector board in-line
# between the actual edge connector and the brs-tester.
#
# On an oscilloscope, trigger off AU and measure AF(ch1) AP(ch2) for the inhibit pulse.
#
####################################################################################
